\section{Columns of \code{records}}{
The first two columns say which input each row came from - \code{source_index} is 1-based in R, so it indexes \code{files} directly - and rows are grouped by input, in input order, whatever \code{threads} is.
\describe{
\item{\code{source_index}}{int; never \code{NA}. 0-based position of the row's input in the stdin list.}
\item{\code{source_path}}{string; never \code{NA}. Absolute path of the row's input.}
\item{\code{sequence}}{string; never \code{NA}. Full sequence with modifications (QuantifiedPeptideFromTsv.Sequence).}
\item{\code{base_sequence}}{string; never \code{NA}. Unmodified sequence.}
\item{\code{peak_order}}{int; \code{NA} when not IsoTracker output: no Peak Order column (then in absent_fields). IsoTracker's peak order.}
\item{\code{protein_groups}}{string; \code{NA} when no Protein Groups column, or a blank cell. Protein groups the peptide maps to, ';'-joined as written.}
\item{\code{gene_names}}{string; \code{NA} when no Gene Names column, or a blank cell. Gene names as written.}
\item{\code{organism}}{string; \code{NA} when no Organism column, or a blank cell. Organism as written.}
\item{\code{sample_label}}{string; \code{NA} when the file has no per-sample columns (then in absent_fields). The sample this row measures.}
\item{\code{intensity}}{float; in \strong{intensity (instrument units)}; \code{NA} when the cell was blank. Intensity_ as written. FlashLFQ writes 0 for a peptide it did not quantify, and 0 crosses as 0: read detection_type.}
\item{\code{detection_type}}{string; \code{NA} when the cell was blank. MSMS, MBR, NotDetected, ... verbatim (Detection Type_).}
\item{\code{retention_time}}{float; in \strong{min}; \code{NA} when not IsoTracker output (then in absent_fields) or a blank cell. RetentionTime (min)_ for this sample.}
}
}
